    "done_when": "The velocity view answers crew(view=\"velocity\") within the crew tool's 30 s read deadline, so it can be read on a real repository. Today one project over two weeks takes 228.5 s: velocity.report replays 3,820 primary commits, 2,314 ledger runs and 547 product commits on every call.\n\nreckon/velocity.py caches each project's captured history, keyed by the repository path and its first-parent head. When the head moves it extends the cache incrementally, capturing only the commits after the cached head. A window read then computes from the cache. The cache lives under the user's cache directory (~/.cache/reckon/velocity/ or its XDG equivalent), outside every repository. It is written through reckon._store.write_json_atomically, and a corrupt or version-mismatched cache entry is rebuilt, never trusted. The report's values are unchanged.\n\nA recorded measurement, not a test, reports these timings on reckon at fc7a5807 for the window 2026-09-15 to 2026-09-29, taken with the same velocity function the MCP view calls:\n- a cold call, with no cache;\n- a warm call at the same head;\n- a warm call after one new commit.\nThe warm figures are under 30 s. The log opens with one line naming its revision, tree and command, and its absolute path is in the manifest with an EXIT= line.\n\ntests/test_velocity_cache.py synthesises repositories under tmp_path and points the cache directory at tmp_path. It asserts:\n- a warm read equals a cold read, value for value;\n- a head that moved is extended, not rebuilt, by counting capture calls;\n- a corrupt cache file is rebuilt.\nNothing is written outside tmp_path. That file, tests/test_velocity.py, tests/test_crew_velocity_view.py and tests/test_crew_velocity_cli.py pass at exit 0. The manifest writes baseline_suite and after_suite each as one line of armed JSON: revision, command with no placeholder, exit_status, completed, failure_count, failure_ids, log_path. The declared negative control is applied and observed to fail, and its log's absolute path is in the manifest with an EXIT= line and the FAILED id.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
    "goal": "Cache each project's captured history by its head so the velocity view answers within the MCP read deadline on a real repository, with values unchanged",
